  "snippet": "Release: datasette-charts 0.2a0 I introduced this new charting plugin for Datasette yesterday. Today it's gained integration with Datasette Agent, so now you can ask chat for a chart and it will create one for you using ...",
  "coverImage": null,
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-charts/releases/tag/0.2a0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-charts 0.2a0</a></p>\n<p>I introduced this new charting plugin for Datasette <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/23/datasette-charts/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">yesterday</a>. Today it's gained integration with <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent</a>, so now you can ask chat for a chart and it will create one for you using the same underlying chart suggestion and generation tools.</p>\n<p>Here's a demo video, recorded on <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">agent.datasette.io</a>  where you can sign in with GitHub to try the plugin yourself:</p>\n<figure>\n<video controls=\"controls\" height=\"1080\" poster=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-charts-agent-demo.webp\" preload=\"none\" style=\"height: auto;\" width=\"1440\">\n<source src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-charts-agent-demo.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"/>\n<a href=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-charts-agent-demo.mp4\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Download the video (MP4)</a>\n</video>\n<figcaption id=\"charts-demo-desc\" style=\"margin-top: 1em;\">\n    I prompt Datasette Agent to \"Use #stats to show sqlite-utils downloads over time as a chart\" - where typing \"#stats\" opens a table search box. It shows me a chart inline in the chat, and when I click \"Open in the chart builder\" it opens the chart in a panel along with the table page. I use the table page to switch to a chart of \"datasette\", then when I ask the agent \"what does the chart show?\" it notices that I changed the content in the panel and describes the new Datasette chart to me.\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>Here's <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/simonw/12646fcc72dddae3d4ac04b496c20af2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">a Markdown export</a> of the chat from the video.</p>\n<p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-agent\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-agent</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/visualization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">visualization</a></p>",
